## 3. Qualified users and permitted purpose

A "Qualified User" is:

- an individual acting solely in an independent academic or educational
  capacity; or
- a public or nonprofit educational or research institution acting solely
  through its employees, faculty members, researchers, or enrolled students.

"Qualified Non-Commercial Research Use" means internal use solely for
independent academic research, scholarly publication, or classroom teaching,
where the use is not undertaken for, on behalf of, at the direction of, or for
the material benefit of a Commercial Entity.

A "Commercial Entity" means any for-profit entity and its affiliates, and any
person or organization acting as its employee, contractor, consultant, agent,
service provider, or research partner for the relevant activity.

Research is not Qualified Non-Commercial Research Use if a Commercial Entity
funds, commissions, directs, controls, receives preferential access to, or
holds commercial rights in the work or its results. General charitable gifts
that create no such rights or control do not, by themselves, disqualify the
research.

## 4. Research license grant

Subject to continuous compliance with this Research License, Licensor grants a
Qualified User a limited, worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive,
non-transferable, and non-sublicensable license to reproduce, install, run, and
modify the Licensed Software solely for Qualified Non-Commercial Research Use.

A qualifying institution may allow its personnel who are Qualified Users to
exercise these rights on systems under that institution's control, provided
that the institution is responsible for their compliance.

Qualified Users may publish scientific results, papers, and data produced by
using the Licensed Software, provided those materials do not contain or
distribute the Licensed Software or a substantial portion of it.

## 5. Uses requiring a commercial license

Unless Licensor has first executed a separate written commercial license, no
person or entity may use the Licensed Software:

- by, for, on behalf of, or for the benefit of a Commercial Entity, including
  internal research, evaluation, benchmarking, proof-of-concept work, or R&D;
- in connection with consulting, contract research, sponsored research,
  fee-for-service work, or any revenue-generating or commercially advantageous
  activity;
- to develop, test, validate, support, operate, or provide a commercial product,
  process, patent, service, or production decision;
- as a hosted, cloud, bureau, platform, or remote-access service;
- in safety-critical or production operations; or
- for any purpose outside Qualified Non-Commercial Research Use.

Commercial scope, fees, support, warranties, and other negotiated terms are
provided only in a separate written agreement or quote. Publication of source
code or possession of a copy does not waive the commercial-license requirement.

